{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44246190",
      "title": "Using the use() Hook for Promises & Data Fetching",
      "sourceHash": "9f61046d69213f72c91d394beb4ba38aaeb9d4287c57132a2463e7517bd9a62c",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 5.73,
          "en": "Now to conclude this theory part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.73,
          "end": 6.84,
          "en": "of this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.84,
          "end": 10.44,
          "en": "there's one last crucial React feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.44,
          "end": 14.043,
          "en": "that you also should understand, and that's the use() hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.94,
          "end": 18.63,
          "en": "Now, you already saw the use() hook in action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.63,
          "end": 20.7,
          "en": "earlier in the course when we used it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.7,
          "end": 23.49,
          "en": "to connect to some context value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.49,
          "end": 27.42,
          "en": "when we used it to access context, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.42,
          "end": 32.42,
          "en": "But it can also be used to await Promises, you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 33.78,
          "end": 37.77,
          "en": "in client components without using Async/await,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 37.77,
          "end": 42.15,
          "en": "which isn't supported there, which might sound strange,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 42.15,
          "end": 45.51,
          "en": "but it is a feature developed by the React team",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 45.51,
          "end": 48.72,
          "en": "that allows you to read values from Promises",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 48.72,
          "end": 52.74,
          "en": "or to wait for Promises to resolve, you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 52.74,
          "end": 56.67,
          "en": "in client components without using async/await.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 56.67,
          "end": 60.45,
          "en": "And it does work together with Suspense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 60.45,
          "end": 62.82,
          "en": "a component offered by React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 62.82,
          "end": 66.12,
          "en": "that helps you with showing a loading fallback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 66.12,
          "end": 67.83,
          "en": "whilst data is being fetched,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 67.83,
          "end": 70.28999999999999,
          "en": "and you'll see it in action soon as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.28999999999999,
          "end": 75.28999999999999,
          "en": "But it actually only works with special kinds of Promises,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 76.05,
          "end": 76.883,
          "en": "you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.883,
          "end": 80.97,
          "en": "not with any random Promise you might create in your code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 80.97,
          "end": 85.59,
          "en": "Instead, this use() hook only wants to work with Promises",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 85.59,
          "end": 88.35,
          "en": "that are in the end created by libraries",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 88.35,
          "end": 92.82,
          "en": "that integrate with React's Suspense feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 92.82,
          "end": 97.08,
          "en": "So Promises ++, you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 97.08,
          "end": 99.72,
          "en": "Promises that behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 99.72,
          "end": 103.92,
          "en": "are built with React's Suspense feature in mind,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 103.92,
          "end": 108.69,
          "en": "and that send certain pieces of information to React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 108.69,
          "end": 109.563,
          "en": "you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 111,
          "end": 116,
          "en": "And again, thankfully, Next.js actually gives you a way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 116.58,
          "end": 118.803,
          "en": "of creating such Promises.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 120.93,
          "end": 125.13,
          "en": "Now for that attached, you'll find another new file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 125.13,
          "end": 128.643,
          "en": "this UsePromisesDemo.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 129.75,
          "end": 134.52,
          "en": "which contains a relatively straightforward React component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 134.52,
          "end": 136.17000000000002,
          "en": "a React server component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 136.17000000000002,
          "end": 139.203,
          "en": "since there is no use client directive in it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 140.43,
          "end": 143.67000000000002,
          "en": "and a component that wants some users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 143.67000000000002,
          "end": 146.163,
          "en": "which are then output down here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 147,
          "end": 149.73,
          "en": "So we could go to the page.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 149.73,
          "end": 154.73,
          "en": "and use this, UsePromiseDemo component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 155.7,
          "end": 159.183,
          "en": "and remove this unused import.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 160.86,
          "end": 165.86,
          "en": "And what you could do now is go to that data fetching demo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 166.2,
          "end": 168.903,
          "en": "and copy that code here, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 169.92000000000002,
          "end": 172.89,
          "en": "and move that into your page.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 172.89,
          "end": 177.63,
          "en": "This is also a server component, so we can use async here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 177.63,
          "end": 181.29,
          "en": "and we can use it to fetch data from that file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 181.29,
          "end": 182.373,
          "en": "That will work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 183.3,
          "end": 188.3,
          "en": "We should just also bring in that fs.import from Node.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 188.4,
          "end": 191.493,
          "en": "so that we have access to this file system module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 192.54,
          "end": 195,
          "en": "While we're in that we're fetching users here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 195,
          "end": 197.91,
          "en": "and we can then set that users prop here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 197.91,
          "end": 200.1,
          "en": "on this UsePromiseDemo component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 200.1,
          "end": 201.903,
          "en": "and pass our users to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 203.01,
          "end": 205.44,
          "en": "And if you do that, if you reload your page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 205.44,
          "end": 207.48,
          "en": "you see all these users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 207.48,
          "end": 210.45,
          "en": "including the ones I added over the last lectures",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 210.45,
          "end": 212.16,
          "en": "here on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 212.16,
          "end": 214.563,
          "en": "So that works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 215.97,
          "end": 220.2,
          "en": "But this approach here has one potential downside.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 220.2,
          "end": 223.35,
          "en": "Let's say we have a slow server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 223.35,
          "end": 226.23,
          "en": "where reading that data and fetching that data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 226.23,
          "end": 227.82,
          "en": "takes a while.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 227.82,
          "end": 232.82,
          "en": "And to simulate this, I'll await a new Promise here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 233.16,
          "end": 238.16,
          "en": "which will actually resolve after a timer expired,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 239.07,
          "end": 240.933,
          "en": "so let's say after two seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 242.1,
          "end": 246.39,
          "en": "Now if I go back here and I click this reload button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 246.39,
          "end": 249.843,
          "en": "it takes two seconds until this page reloads.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 250.77,
          "end": 255.21,
          "en": "And this is even easier to see if I open a new tab.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 255.21,
          "end": 259.263,
          "en": "It takes two seconds until anything appears on the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 260.94,
          "end": 264.42,
          "en": "That's of course not necessarily a great user experience.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 264.42,
          "end": 267.63,
          "en": "And the reason for that is that I'm fetching the data here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 267.63,
          "end": 269.07,
          "en": "in the page.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 269.07,
          "end": 272.7,
          "en": "and therefore this entire page content is only rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 272.7,
          "end": 274.173,
          "en": "once the data is there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 276.3,
          "end": 280.09000000000003,
          "en": "Now, one way around that would be to grab that code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 281.28,
          "end": 284.85,
          "en": "and remove it from this home component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 284.85,
          "end": 286.32,
          "en": "from this page.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 286.32,
          "end": 289.983,
          "en": "and put it into this UsePromisesDemo.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 291.36,
          "end": 294.48,
          "en": "For that, we need to add Async here, which we can,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 294.48,
          "end": 297.03,
          "en": "since it's a server component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 297.03,
          "end": 301.053,
          "en": "and we have to bring over that fs import.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 303.12,
          "end": 305.37,
          "en": "Now the users are fetched here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 305.37,
          "end": 308.283,
          "en": "therefore we no longer need that prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 309.33,
          "end": 313.71,
          "en": "And in the page.js file, we no longer need to pass anything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 313.71,
          "end": 315.273,
          "en": "to UsePromiseDemo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 316.35,
          "end": 318.99,
          "en": "Now with that alone, nothing would change though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 318.99,
          "end": 320.88,
          "en": "If I copy that and open a new tab,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 320.88,
          "end": 324.123,
          "en": "it still takes two seconds until we see anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 325.41,
          "end": 329.37,
          "en": "But we could now use a feature built into React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 329.37,
          "end": 333.6,
          "en": "that allows us to wrap a part of our JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 333.6,
          "end": 335.94,
          "en": "that might take a bit longer to load",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 335.94,
          "end": 340.8,
          "en": "and show a fallback without blocking any other JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 340.8,
          "end": 342.933,
          "en": "or any other content from loading.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 344.19,
          "end": 347.01,
          "en": "And that would be the Suspense component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 347.01,
          "end": 348.78,
          "en": "that's built into React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 348.78,
          "end": 350.28,
          "en": "and that you already saw",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 350.28,
          "end": 353.883,
          "en": "in the context of lazy loading earlier in the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 355.05,
          "end": 358.89,
          "en": "Suspense is a component that's provided by React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 358.89,
          "end": 361.89,
          "en": "that can be wrapped around any content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 361.89,
          "end": 363.753,
          "en": "that is loading something.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 365.04,
          "end": 367.39,
          "en": "That something could be code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 367.39,
          "end": 370.11,
          "en": "if you're using it for lazy loading,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 370.11,
          "end": 372.87,
          "en": "but it can also be data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 372.87,
          "end": 375.966,
          "en": "if that data fetching is done in a way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 375.966,
          "end": 378.72,
          "en": "that works with Suspense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 378.72,
          "end": 381.09,
          "en": "which is the case in Next.js projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 381.09,
          "end": 384.54,
          "en": "when working with React server components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 384.54,
          "end": 388.26,
          "en": "So to put it in other words, React server components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 388.26,
          "end": 391.83,
          "en": "that fetch data do integrate with Suspense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 391.83,
          "end": 393.87,
          "en": "and can be wrapped by it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 393.87,
          "end": 396.36,
          "en": "It won't work with all components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 396.36,
          "end": 399.363,
          "en": "but it will work with React server components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 400.62,
          "end": 403.29,
          "en": "Suspense then takes a fallback prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 403.29,
          "end": 407.28,
          "en": "and this can be used to define some fallback markup",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 407.28,
          "end": 411.123,
          "en": "that should be shown whilst the data is being fetched here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 412.8,
          "end": 415.44,
          "en": "As a result of using Suspense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 415.44,
          "end": 419.01,
          "en": "you will see that now the page loads instantly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 419.01,
          "end": 421.923,
          "en": "and we see that fallback until the data appears,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 422.79,
          "end": 425.52,
          "en": "and that's of course a better user experience",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 425.52,
          "end": 427.14,
          "en": "than what we had before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 427.14,
          "end": 430.293,
          "en": "where the entire page took two seconds to load.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 431.49,
          "end": 435.54,
          "en": "But how is this now related to the use() hook?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 435.54,
          "end": 437.703,
          "en": "Well, that's what we'll explore next.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}